This file exists so that the //go:embed patterns in assets.go and
assets_test.go always have something to match.

Without it, `go build ./...` and `go test ./...` fail on a fresh clone with

    pattern all:ui/out: no matching files found

which says nothing about the real cause: the frontend has not been built yet.
go:embed is resolved at compile time and needs at least one matching file, so a
placeholder is the only way to keep the Go toolchain usable before
`pnpm build:ui` has run.

The name deliberately does not start with a dot. A plain `//go:embed ui/out`
(which assets_test.go uses to prove the `all:` prefix is necessary) skips
dot-prefixed files, so a .gitkeep here would leave that pattern with nothing to
match and break the build in a second, more confusing way.

The real bundle lands beside this file and is gitignored. assets_test.go skips
itself when only this placeholder is present, and says what to run.
